    <!-- Principles -->
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="values-heading">
      <header class="section-header">
        <h2 id="values-heading" class="hs">How I Work</h2>
        <p class="section-subtitle">Six principles that guide how I approach product and analysis work</p>
      </header>
      <div class="principles-grid">
        <article class="principle-card">
          <div class="principle-icon" aria-hidden="true">◆</div>
          <h3>Clarity Before Code</h3>
          <p>Backend-heavy systems hide risk in edge cases. I turn open questions into agreed scenarios before build — rework in AI is expensive.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle-card">
          <h3>Make Status Visible</h3>
          <p>Every handoff should show where it stands — in the product and in Jira, not in messages that get missed.</        </article>
        <article class="principle-card">
          <h3>Keep Scope Honest</h3>
          <p>Infrastructure, extras, and new ideas become visible change requests with estimates. The client always knows what they're choosing.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle-card">
          <h3>Write It Down</h3>
          <p>Requirements, flow designs, and user manuals are living documents with version history. Knowledge shouldn't leave when people do.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle-card">
          <h3>Plan Around Dependencies</h3>
          <p>Specs, credentials, and test environments often come from third parties. I track them as dated risks with owners.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle-card">
          <h3>Prototype to Align</h3>
          <p>I wireframe and build small prototypes so conversations with ML engineers, infra teams, and designers stay concrete.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

